<item><title>Tunisia calls for roadmap to recycle construction waste in roads</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/tn/tunisia-calls-for-roadmap-to-recycle-construction-waste-in-aec176/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/tn/tunisia-calls-for-roadmap-to-recycle-construction-waste-in-aec176/</guid><category>Tunisia</category><description>The government says future road projects could use 20 to 30% recycled material, while a trial on the RN3 tests durability.</description><pubDate>Sat, 28 Nov 2026 09:35:41 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/tn.jpg" length="31271" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/tn.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>United ATS opens Tunis aviation training centre for regional clients</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/tn/united-ats-opens-tunis-aviation-training-centre-for-367a43/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/tn/united-ats-opens-tunis-aviation-training-centre-for-367a43/</guid><category>Tunisia</category><description>The company says local training, priced in Tunisian dinars, can replace services that aviation customers currently buy abroad.</description><pubDate>Sat, 28 Nov 2026 07:10:03 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/tn.jpg" length="31271" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/tn.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Solar industry body urges Tunisia to revisit rejected tax cuts</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/tn/solar-industry-body-urges-tunisia-to-revisit-rejected-tax-252dcc/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/tn/solar-industry-body-urges-tunisia-to-revisit-rejected-tax-252dcc/</guid><category>Tunisia</category><description>The photovoltaic chamber wants lawmakers to reconsider lower import duties on solar panels and exemptions for storage batteries in the 2027 finance bill.</description><pubDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 17:50:47 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/tn.jpg" length="31271" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/tn.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Tunisian olive growers say oil must sell for 15 dinars a litre to cover costs</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/tn/tunisian-olive-growers-say-oil-must-sell-for-15-dinars-a-ff0538/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/tn/tunisian-olive-growers-say-oil-must-sell-for-15-dinars-a-ff0538/</guid><category>Tunisia</category><description>Midani Dhaoui, head of the Tunisian farmers&apos; union, says rising costs and falling olive prices are squeezing producers.</description><pubDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 13:13:27 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/tn/tunisian-olive-growers-say-oil-must-sell-for-15-dinars-a-ff0538/share.jpg" length="44173" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/tn/tunisian-olive-growers-say-oil-must-sell-for-15-dinars-a-ff0538/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
